course: dictionary
lesson: 11312
title: Cries and sudden sounds
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can be a doing word (verb) or a thing word (noun). «Chloe yelped and burst into tears.» Yelped is a doing word: Chloe made a short, sharp cry. Tears come after the cry, so the cry was probably caused by pain or fright.
explain: The same word can be a noun too. In the sentence «The puppy gave a yelp when someone trod on its paw», yelp is the thing that was made. Notice the words «a» and «when someone trod on its paw»: they are the clues that tell you what happened.
explain: Look at the sentence around the word. Ask yourself: what would make someone do that? Then swap in your meaning, a short, sharp cry, and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Yelp (verb) means to give a short, sharp cry, especially of pain, fright or surprise.
fact: A yelp (noun) is a short, sharp cry, especially from a dog or a person.
fact: The verb forms are yelp, yelps, yelped and yelping. Use yelped for something that happened in the past.
fact: «Chloe yelped and burst into tears.» Here yelped shows a sudden cry, probably from pain or fright.
fact: «The scream heard on winter nights is often a fox calling to find a mate or mark its patch; foxes also bark, yelp and chatter.» Here yelp is one of the sounds a fox can make.
exercise: «Chloe yelped and burst into tears.» What does yelped mean? | Ran away quietly | Sang a long, happy song | *Gave a short, sharp cry | Fell fast asleep
exercise: A puppy gives a yelp when someone treads on its paw. What is a yelp? | A kind of paw print | A soft, slow yawn | *A short, sharp cry, often of pain | A bark that goes on for hours
exercise: «Chloe yelped and burst into tears.» Why do you think she yelped? | *Because something hurt or frightened her | Because she was winning a race | Because it was her birthday | Because she was bored
test: Yesterday the dog ___ when the door slammed shut. Which word fits? | yelps | yelp | yelping | *yelped
test: Mo heard a yelp from the kitchen. What is a yelp in this sentence? | A loud, sharp cry | A long, quiet song | A kind of biscuit | *A short, sharp cry
exam: Which sentence uses yelp as a noun, a thing? | The puppy yelped when it was stepped on. | *The puppy gave a sharp yelp when it was stepped on. | The puppy is yelping by the door. | The puppy yelps every morning at breakfast.
